      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cook the pasta"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oven to 200 degrees C. Cook {{pasta-dried}} of pasta in a large pan of salted boiling water for 2 minutes less than the packet time. It will finish cooking in the oven. Drain and set aside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the cheese sauce"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Melt {{unsalted-butter}} of butter in a medium saucepan over medium heat. Add {{plain-flour}} of plain flour all at once and stir for 1 to 2 minutes until the mixture smells biscuity."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add {{whole-milk}} of warm milk a little at a time, whisking after each addition to keep the sauce smooth. Once all the milk is in, cook for 4 to 5 minutes, stirring, until thick enough to coat the back of a spoon well."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove from the heat. Stir in {{cheddar}} of grated cheddar and {{dijon-mustard}} of mustard if using. Season well."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assemble and bake"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Tip the drained pasta into the baking dish. Add {{tuna-tinned}} of drained tuna, broken into chunks, and {{sweetcorn-tinned}} of drained sweetcorn. Pour over the cheese sauce and stir gently to combine."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Scatter extra grated cheddar and {{breadcrumbs-dried}} of breadcrumbs over the top if using. Bake for 20 to 25 minutes until the top is golden and the sauce is bubbling at the edges."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "rows": [
            {
              "symptom": "Sauce is lumpy",
              "cause": "Milk added too fast or sauce not whisked constantly",
              "fix": "Push through a sieve and return to the pan. Next time, add the milk in small additions and whisk between each one."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Bake is dry after cooking",
              "cause": "Sauce was too thin before baking or pasta was overcooked first",
              "fix": "The sauce should be quite thick before it goes in the oven. Par-cook the pasta so it finishes in the oven, not before."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Top is pale and not golden",
              "cause": "Oven not hot enough or baked too briefly",
              "fix": "Switch to the grill for the last 3 to 4 minutes and watch carefully. The breadcrumbs and cheddar brown quickly."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Tuna is dry and stringy",
              "cause": "Tuna in brine used rather than in oil, or baked too long",
              "fix": "Tuna in oil stays moister through baking. Break it into large chunks so pieces stay tender."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tuna pasta bake became a British staple in the 1980s and 1990s as tinned tuna grew popular and pasta moved into mainstream home cooking. It sits alongside chicken casserole and shepherd's pie as a dish British families make on rotation. Each household has its own slight version. Pasta, white sauce, tinned fish, and melted cheese: it belongs to the same family as macaroni cheese and fish pie. Filling, reliable, and made from what is in the cupboard."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
